Ladybird’s network event actors now outlive the frame target that was
current when their requests started. In Firefox, they never belonged
to a frame target: The NetworkEventWatcher that the WatcherActor runs
in the parent process creates them, so replacing a frame target leaves
the page’s requests alone.

Run headless with a server that answers a POST two seconds after the
page loads, the POST now gets its 501 status and its body, and before,
it got neither, and every request of the page answered unknownActor. The
page’s own document request still gets no completion update, since Fetch
never reports that request as finished; that’s outside DevTools.
